# No client-side polling without approval

Before implementing any of the following, **ask the user first** and wait for explicit approval:

- `setInterval` / `setTimeout` loops that call APIs
- Background session refresh or status polling (e.g. every N seconds)
- Automatic retry loops on lifecycle or approval screens
- Any pattern that scales as `(active users × poll frequency)` API load

## Preferred patterns for status checks

- **Manual button** — user clicks to refresh (e.g. "Check approval status")
- **Re-login** — fresh session on sign-in after ops action
- **Server push** — email, webhook, or WebSocket (discuss with user before building)

## Rationale

Polling from many concurrent hospital admins (e.g. thousands on pending-approval) creates unnecessary load on CureFlow APIs. Manual or event-driven flows are the default.
